# SoundCloud Desktop (custom edition)

An unofficial desktop app for [SoundCloud](https://soundcloud.com) built with Electron. It adds themes, optional plugins, Discord Rich Presence, a tray icon, media-key support and a floating mini player.

> Not affiliated with or endorsed by SoundCloud.

## Requirements

- Windows 10/11
- [Node.js](https://nodejs.org) (LTS version)
- Git (optional, only to clone the repo)

## Run it

1. Download the repo (**Code → Download ZIP**, then extract it) or clone it:

   ```powershell
   git clone https://github.com/<your-username>/<your-repo>.git
   cd <your-repo>
   ```

2. Install the dependencies and start the app:

   ```powershell
   npm install
   npm start
   ```

   The first `npm install` takes a minute because it downloads Electron.

3. Log in to SoundCloud inside the app and play something.

## Using it

- Click the **gear icon** to open Settings. There you can pick a theme and turn plugins on or off. Settings save automatically.
- Right-click the **tray icon** for quick toggles: theme, plugins, Discord Rich Presence, ad/tracker blocking and minimize-to-tray.
- Closing the window hides it to the tray (you can turn this off). Use **Quit** in the tray menu to fully exit.
- Media keys (play/pause, next, previous) work even when the app is in the background.

## Features

- **Themes:** Gold, Galaxy, OLED Black, Sakura, Dracula, Nord, Catppuccin, Synthwave, Forest and more, plus a custom theme you create yourself.
- **Discord Rich Presence:** shows the current song on your Discord profile, with an optional progress bar, artwork and a "Listen on SoundCloud" button. Discord must be open on the same computer.
- **Plugins** (all optional):
  - Compact library
  - Focus mode
  - Soft corners
  - Accent glow
  - Theme creator
  - Listening history (stored locally)
  - Volume memory
  - Keyboard shortcuts: Space play/pause, ←/→ seek, M mute, N/P next/previous
  - Audio visualizer
  - Track notifications
  - Floating player (always-on-top, draggable and resizable)

Plugins are local and CSS-based. They don't load remote code or automate SoundCloud actions.

## Build a portable .exe

```powershell
npm run build
```

The portable executable is created in the `dist` folder.

## Customising

- **Add a theme:** add an entry in `themes.js`. It appears in Settings and the tray menu automatically.
- **Add a CSS plugin:** add an entry in `plugins.js`. It appears in Settings and the tray menu automatically.

## Troubleshooting

| Problem | Fix |
| --- | --- |
| `npm` is not recognized | Install Node.js, then open a new terminal window. |
| App window doesn't open | Run `npm install` again, then `npm start`. |
| Discord status doesn't show | Make sure the Discord desktop app is open and Rich Presence is on in Settings. Also check Discord's **Settings → Activity Privacy** setting. |
| Closing the window doesn't quit | It minimizes to the tray. Use the tray menu's **Quit**, or turn off minimize-to-tray. |
| A page looks broken after a change | Ad/tracker blocking is on by default. Turn it off in the tray menu and restart the app. |
